    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-17923" textLabel="gibberellin 2β,3β-hydroxylase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q94IE3" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="536.0499267578125" centerY="1160.176513671875" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, dreher">GA3ox1 is a multifunctional protein involved in gibberellin metabolism in rice. It can act as a gibberellin 3&amp;beta;-hydroxylase (for example, by catalyzing the conversion of |FRAME: CPD-15217 gibberellin A&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;| to |FRAME: GIBBERELLIN gibberellin A&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;|)), as a 2,3-desaturase (by catalzying the transformation of |FRAME: CPD1F-140 gibberellin A&lt;sub&gt;20&lt;/sub&gt;| to |FRAME: CPD-15217 gibberellin A&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;|), and as a gibberellin 2&amp;beta;-hydroxylase by catalyzing the conversion of |FRAME: CPD1F-139 gibberellin A&lt;sub&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt;| to |FRAME: CPD-204 gibberellin A&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;| &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [11438692]|. It is a member of the 2-oxoglutarate-dependent dioxygenase family of proteins. GA3ox1 transcript levels are highest in unopened flowers |CITS: [11438692]|.</Comment>
